# Architecture

<!-- awf:section overview stub -->
## Overview

awf renders one standard workflow footprint from committed `.awf/` configuration. The Go CLI validates, renders, and checks that configuration; generated target artifacts provide the agent-facing workflow. Its resident-data boundaries keep local effort and worktree state outside managed output.{{ with .commitPolicy }} Commit-policy configuration is consumed by the architecture's verification boundary.{{ end }}
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section components stub -->
## Components

- `cmd/awf`: CLI composition root for parsing, invoking focused operations, presenting results, and mapping exits.
- `internal/project`: `Loader` opens and validates selected project state to construct one immutable `Session`.
- `internal/outputplan` and `internal/publisher`: immutable output plans and the `Publisher` that owns output planning, rendering coordination, ownership and collision preflight, and lock-last publication without effect or recovery ledgers.
- `internal/repositorycheck` and focused check owners: the policy-free `RepositoryChecker` preserves ordered aggregation, while each concern owner retains its classification, severity, and policy.
- Focused operation packages: directly compose writer leases, confined authority access, fresh committed Session reload, and one-attempt Publisher synchronization while owning validation, ordered mutation, ownership policy, affected-path outcomes, release handling, and presentation. Earlier successful effects are not rolled back.
- `internal/topic` and `internal/currentstate`: live-authority parsing and checks.
- `internal/effort` and `internal/worktree`: local effort residents and Git-backed topology.
- `internal/git`: the sole semantic Git boundary.
- Harness outputs: Claude and Pi each receive only `awf-effort`, `awf-topics`, `awf-decisions`, and `awf-maintenance`. Operator-installed `agentic-skills` owns generic skills, canonical roles, and its Pi adapter; separately installed `pi-tools` owns Pi role execution and runtime mechanics. AWF emits no role prompts, adapter, router, policy, or preference store.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section data-flow stub -->
## Data flow

A command loads `.awf/`, derives an output plan, and renders or checks the managed files. Mutations acquire a writer lease before mutable-authority reads, protect paths without sufficient ownership evidence, completely preflight every collision and destructive path they can derive, and write `.awf/awf.lock` last. Git-backed multi-file changes are ordered rather than transactional: a failure stops at the first failed mutation and reports affected paths for inspection and rerun. Current-state checks read working or staged authority; audit reads selected committed history through `internal/git`. Effort residents and worktrees remain local state outside rendered output.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section dependencies stub -->
## Key dependencies

| Dependency | Role |
|---|---|
| `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` | Strict configuration and frontmatter parsing. |
| `text/template` | Rendering. |
| `github.com/go-git/go-git/v5` and Git | Git seam backends. |
| `github.com/bmatcuk/doublestar/v4` | Anchored path glob matching. |
| Pi APIs | Adopter-supplied runtime APIs for awf-owned outputs, not CLI dependencies. |
| `agentic-skills` | Operator-installed generic skills, canonical roles, and harness packaging; never an AWF binary dependency. |
| `pi-tools` | Separately operator-installed Pi role execution and runtime mechanics; never installed or probed by AWF. |
<!-- awf:end -->